  "body": "## What was broken\n\nEvery \\`install.sh --version <pin>\\` died at the checksum step. The pinned path intentionally ships no digest (\"No release feed is read for an explicit version\"), but the downloader compared unconditionally — guaranteed \\`checksum mismatch\\`. Two audit-probe-confirmed secondary defects rode along: the digest extractor never reset its asset scope, so a target asset published without a digest borrowed the NEXT asset's digest; and the comment describing GitHub's body/assets position was inverted.\n\n## The fix\n\n- Pinned installs now fetch the **tag-scoped feed** (\\`releases/tags/v<version>\\`) so they stay **verified**; only an unreachable feed downgrades to an explicitly-warned unverified download; a readable feed that omits the wheel's own digest refuses loudly rather than trusting anything.\n- \\`extract_wheel_digest\\` hard-scopes awk to the matched asset object: name-match opens the scope, the asset's own \\`browser_download_url\\` closes it, and release-body prose can never satisfy it.\n- Corrected the inverted comments (script + fixture); four new scenarios cover pinned-verified / unreachable-feed-proceeds-unverified / missing-digest-refused-despite-sibling / latest-path regression.\n\n## Verification\n\nOffline PATH-shimmed replica (curl/sha256sum/fixtures): PASS x5 incl. all four scenarios. §66 mutations x3, each caught by name, restores asserted byte-identical. \\`ruff format/check\\`, \\`ty\\` green. Whole-file \\`pytest tests/scripts/test_installers.py\\`: 50 passed, 20 skipped, **8 failed — reproduced identically at clean base via stash roundtrip** (pre-existing PowerShell-harness failures, documented local baseline). POSIX pytest scenarios self-skip on Windows hosts by design; on Linux CI the four new sh scenarios execute for real. Version: PATCH bump to 5.51.1 included (production path).\n\n## Residual risks\n\nPinned installs add one GitHub API call (rate-limit friendly). The unverified fallback prints warnings to stderr only — if an operator pipes stderr away, the downgrade is quieter than ideal; acceptable for an explicitly requested pin.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
