    },
    "message": "fix(installer): make pinned --version installs verifiable instead of always failing\n\nBroken: `install.sh --version X` deliberately shipped no digest (\"No release\nfeed is read for an explicit version\") while download_verified_release_wheel\ncompared the hash unconditionally, so every pinned install died with\n\"checksum mismatch\". Secondary defect: the awk digest extractor never reset\nin_asset, so a target asset published without a digest borrowed the NEXT\nasset's; comments in install.sh and the test docstring also claimed GitHub\nplaces the release body before assets -- reality is inverted (body follows).\n\nFix: a pinned install now reads the tag-scoped feed\n(api.github.com/.../releases/tags/v<version>) and stays verified; if the feed\nis unreachable it fails open loudly (\"could not reach ... proceeding\nunverified\" + \"WITHOUT checksum verification\" before the install) instead of\nrefusing; if a readable feed omits the wheel asset's own digest it refuses\nloudly (\"No digest published for this asset\"). Digest extraction moved to a\nshared extract_wheel_digest() whose scope ends at every non-matching \"name\"\nline and at the asset's browser_download_url, so sibling digests and release-\nbody prose can never satisfy the wheel. download_verified_release_wheel grew\nan explicit unverified branch reachable only from that fallback. Corrected\nthe inverted body/assets comments in both files; the POSIX curl shim gained\nan fcc-feed failure branch; added four scenarios: pinned verified via tag\nfeed (never touching /releases/latest), pinned unverified on unreachable\nfeed, pinned no-target-digest refusal (sibling-with-digest present), and the\nlatest-path no-digest refusal sharing the guard.\n\nVerification: sh -n OK; ruff format --check / ruff check / ty clean;\nwhole-file pytest tests/scripts/test_installers.py: 50 passed, 20 skipped,\n8 failed -- all 8 are PowerShell-harness failures reproduced identically at\nthe clean base via stash roundtrip (pre-existing, outside this lane's\nsurface); offline PATH-shimmed PosixHarness replica passes the latest-path\nregression plus all four new scenarios; mutation checks per the section 66\nlaw: awk-scope-reset -> case-c refused-borrowed-digest fails by name,\nmissing-digest-refusal -> cases c+d fail by name, downloader-unverified-gate\n-> case-a fails by name; installer bytes restored identical after mutations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
